  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 122 PM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nLittle substantive change is expected in the weather over the next \nseveral days. Conditions remain hot and opportunities for rain will \nbe hard to come by as ridging strengthens over the area. Afternoon \nbreezes are expected to trend downward after Friday as high pressure \nover the Gulf broadens. A weak inverted trough is forecast to \nmove onshore South Texas on Friday. The increase in moisture may \nbe accompanied by isolated showers from the Coastal Plains to \nWinter Garden region, though rain chances are low (below 30 \npercent). That may be our only window for rain within the next 10 \ndays. The more noteworthy change is that the passing disturbance \ncould raise heat indices by a few degrees, especially over the \nCoastal Plains and I35 corridor where conditions could meet Heat \nAdvisory criteria. Moisture is expected to decrease over the \nweekend into next week, but hot weather will continue to prevail \nwith highs regularly straddling 100F.",
